# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEVER commit these: they can contain live secret material.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Private working folder used mid-run. The exporter deletes it on success, but
# an interrupted run can leave raw, unredacted ARM behind.
exports/**/.work/
**/.work/

# Only produced when output.keepRawExport = true: the unredacted export straight
# from Azure, connection strings and keys included.
exports/**/raw-unsanitised/
**/raw-unsanitised/

# Filled-in parameter files. The generated *.sample.* files are safe to commit;
# a copy with real values is not.
*.parameters.json
!*.parameters.sample.json
*.bicepparam
!*.sample.bicepparam

# Local config variants, which may name environments, subscriptions or tenants.
# config/export.config.json itself IS tracked.
config/*.local.json
config/export.config.*.json
!config/export.config.json

# Anything a credential could land in.
*.publishsettings
*.pubxml
*.pfx
*.p12
*.key
*.pem
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
azureauth.json
*.azureauth

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated output
#
# Exports are IGNORED here because this is the tool's own repo - runs against
# real subscriptions should not land in it. To use git as a drift log, point
# -OutputPath at a SEPARATE audit repo and use -GitCommit there. See the README,
# "Tracking drift in git".
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
exports/
azure-audit/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor / OS / tooling noise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.claude/settings.local.json
graft/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
